  "details": "There are inconsistencies about the name of the \"Early Supporter\" / \"Early Adopter\" badge. Both phrases are used across strings and other official media.\n\nI gathered all strings and official sources I could find.\n\nIt seems like the \"Early Supporter\" term is consistent across marketing assets like articles/updates, images and videos.\n\n# Strings:\n\n*Early Supporter:*\n\n- \"Early Supporters earned me as a badge!\" (https://crowdin.com/editor/vrchat-application/19/en-pl?view=comfortable&filter=basic&value=0#22257)\n\n- \"Thanks for being an Early Supporter!\" (https://crowdin.com/editor/vrchat-application/19/en-pl?view=comfortable&filter=basic&value=0#22255)\n\n*Early Adopter:*\n\n- \"Early Adopter Badge\" (https://crowdin.com/editor/vrchat-application/19/en-pl?view=comfortable&filter=basic&value=0#13707)\n\n# Other sources:\n\n*Early Supporter:*\n\n- VRChat+ launch article (https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/438100/view/2905347189759891799)\n\n- Badge launch video (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kc_1IBX8bUw)\n\n- Reminder article about the badge going away soon, text + graphic (https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/438100/view/3673283222240781051)\n\n*Early Adopter:*\n\n- Badge icon alt text on the website on the profile\n\n*Early Supporter & Early Adopter:*\n\n- Reminder post, \"Supporter\" on graphic, \"Adopter\" in text (https://twitter.com/VRChat/status/1616533150661836832)",
